# Field validation — live UI and required coverage

When writing or rewriting a proceso field-validation report, score what both screens do, not what the JSP always renders or what an Angular enum comment claims. Depth to match: `model-result/32515/filed-validation/report.md`.

Do not file **Incorrect** or **Missing** until all of these are true:

- Old **JavaScript** for that field was opened (`change`, `show`/`hide`/`display`, `disabled`, jquery `validate` `rules`). A `c:if` / `mostrar*` flag only means the control exists in markup.
- New `validadores.tipo` is a type `formas-dinamicas` actually applies (`pattern`, `required`, `minlength`, `customMaxlength`). `pattren` and other typos never run.
- One typed example was checked. If both UIs keep `ABC-01`, the row is **Match** even if a comment says alphanumeric-only.

Typical live-UI matches that markup-only scoring gets wrong:

- Field in JSP, hidden by JS until a catalog value (Otro uso / `#divOtrosUso`).
- País catalog in JSP, locked to `MEX` + `disabled` for nacional destinatario (`muestraCamposNacional`).
- Optional text in JSP, jquery `{ minlength: 5, maxlength: 5, digits: true }` on save.
- `display:none` whose `.show()` is commented → **Correctly absent**, not Missing (RFC on 220103).

Every report must include these types (Match when they agree; do not skip a type):

- Every tab label and every section heading (Kind `Text`)
- Every catalog empty option: old `nonSelectionText` versus new `marcadorDePosicion` / catalogo-select default `Seleccione una opción`
- Readonly versus disabled (`readonly="true"` is not `desactivado`)
- Parent catalogs: child loads from parent and clears when parent changes
- Paste on every filtered field (stay in the box and whether Continuar/Agregar saves it)
- Continuar from another tab (validators on tabs that are not open)
- Shared Solicitante / session block under Only in the migrated form on registration
- Required, maxlength, keypress, pattern, message, on-failure, show/hide, enable/disable
